":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.16315472795818553,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.0036656220103203074,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":53.7,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.08139155836110504,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.036187303110615354,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":95.2,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.08854,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":59.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"TotalEnergies SE, an integrated energy company, produces and markets oil and biofuels, natural gas, biogas and low-carbon hydrogen, renewables, and electricity in France, the United States, Europe, Africa, and internationally. It operates through Exploration & Production, Integrated LNG, Integrated Power, Refining & Chemicals, and Marketing & Services segments. The Exploration & Production segment engages in the activities of exploration and production of oil and natural gas, as well as carbon storage. The Integrated LNG segment is involved in the upstream and midstream LNG activities, as well as biogas and synthetic methane activities, as well as gas trading. The Integrated Power segment engages in the generation, storage, electricity trading, and B2B-B2C distribution of gas and electricity. The Refining & Chemicals segment is involved in the industrial hub activities comprising the activities of refining, petrochemicals and specialty chemicals. This segment also includes the activities of oil supply, trading and marine shipping, as well as hydrogen activities. The Marketing & Services segment engages in the marketing activities in the field of petroleum products, as well as corresponding supply and logistics activities. The company was formerly known as TOTAL SE and changed its name to TotalEnergies SE in June 2021. TotalEnergies SE was incorporated in 1924 and is headquartered in Courbevoie, France.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Patrick  Pouyanne | Chairman & CEO | Age 62 | Compensation: $4.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 94K people. Revenue per employee of $2.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Energy peers. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["TotalEnergies SE is a large-cap energy business with a $199.0B market cap on $201.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -11% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage runs at 8.3\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 8.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 8.9% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.11554266482924622},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Energy peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 33% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","34 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Fisher Asset Management LLC Sells 564,644 Shares of TotalEnergies SE Sponsored ADR $TTE","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/fisher-asset-management-llc-sells-564644-shares-of-totalenergies-se-sponsored-adr-tte.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794562638.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.954,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The Zacks Analyst Blog Highlights Home Depot, Gilead Sciences, TotalEnergies, Key Tronic and iPower","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029170/the-zacks-analyst-blog-highlights-home-depot-gilead-sciences-totalenergies-key-tronic-and-ipower?cid=CS-ZC-FT-press_releases-3029170","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794552660.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Top Research Reports for Home Depot, Gilead & TotalEnergies","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/commentary/3028724/top-rese